 "hinweis": "Single source of the insert vocabulary (package 1.10 slice 4). Generated from this file by djk/contract/generate_insert.py: djk/core/signalbox/src/insert_zeilen.inc and djk/ui/project/insert_schluessel.ts. Never edit those by hand. Paths are '<praefix>/<n>/<gruppe><m>/<name>' or '<praefix>/<n>/<name>', at most 31 characters. 'tabelle' says whether the kind has rows in the controller table yet (komp from 4a, eq/saett from 4b, rack from 4c, lim from the master limiter, host from plan 1.11 T4, utility from arr-fx: width, bass mono, gain and balance, 0 samples of latency, the 1.15 Utility module, bk from arr-bk: a Baukasten effect graph with the knobs k1..k8, 0..1, default 0.5; the instance smooths a changed knob over 20 ms itself, so rampe_ms is 0). 'latenz' is the latency in samples a stage of the kind adds at 48 kHz (the delay compensation of the arrangement, slice 4b T13; pinned to cypher_*_latenz() by test_arr_pdc; host: 0 here because the latency of a foreign plugin is a property of the stage, ArrStufe::latenz from the playback file, plan 1.11 D4; bk: 0 here because the latency of a graph is a property of the stage too, measured from the instance by the loader (cypher_bk_latenz), at most 128 samples; lim: 74 samples, pinned to KanalLimiter(48000, {vorhalt 1.5 ms, sample peak}).latenz_samples()); 'instanzen' is the pool size; for eq and saett it was decided by the cost measurement (slice 4b T11, docs/architecture/stand/routing-1-10.md), not guessed; the other kinds only contribute their paths to the vocabulary. 'geraet' is the plugin parameter id in djk/ui/presets/devices.ts ('<n>' is the band number); null where the plugin has no such parameter. Units and ranges are the plugin's. Curve 'schalter' = switch, 'stufen' = integer steps, 'linear' = continuous (kurven as in controls.h KurvenTyp).",
